{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HRe5yrkDv6bT1k9xy6KvNe","type":"tool_result","content":"9:## Quick start (a complete game)\n40:## Look target (read this before drawing anything)\n53:## Coordinates: what x, y, z mean in each view\n69:## Rules\n78:## Common mistakes (check these first)\n86:## Game\n102:## Scenes (title, play, game over)\n113:## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\n129:## Standard features (every game has them: don't build your own)\n136:## Input: `game.input`\n146:## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\n155:## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\n164:## Sound: `game.audio` (chip synth, no files, starts after the first key press)\n170:## Levels\n182:## Movement and physics\n200:## Characters\n216:## Effects and lighting\n222:## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n262:## More: animation and examples outside this card\n286:## Before you hand the game back\nAPI.md:94:- Methods: `follow(obj, { z: 16, lead: 20 })` (camera tracks it automatically), `focus(x, y, z)` (or aim it yourself every update), `setView(id)`, `nextView()`, `freeze(s)` (hit-stop: `update` waits; `game.hitstop` is the time left), `shake(n)`, `after(s, fn)`, `every(s, fn)` (timers in game time, return `{ cancel() }`), `mouseGround()`, `go(scene, data)`, `enableGPU({ map })`.\nAPI.md:234:| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\nAPI.md:235:| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\nAPI-INDEX.md:221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\nAPI-INDEX.md:223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\nAPI-INDEX.md:497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n166:- Custom: `sfx({ wave: 'square' | 'pulse' | 'pulse12' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'sine' | 'noise', freq: 440 or 'A4', to: 880, dur: .2, vol: .3, arp: [0, 4, 7], step: .05, vib: [8, .03] })`, or `audio.define('zap', voice)`.\n167:- Music: `music('title' | 'adventure' | 'dungeon' | 'boss' | 'victory')` (built in; any other name warns and plays nothing), or your own `{ bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .15, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 . . . | ...' }, { wave: 'triangle', notes: '...' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] }`. Tokens: a note (`C4`, `F#3`, `Bb2`), `-` holds, `.` rests, `|` is ignored; drums `k s h o c t`. `music(null)` stops. `mute()`, `setVolume(0..1)` (or set `audio.musicVolume`, `sfxVolume`, then `audio.applyVolume()`), `duck(on)` (quieter music under your own pause or map screen).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"213edd46-9651-46f8-a282-da1d89430eab","uuid":"451ff6ea-4faa-441a-aa8c-a7822e4ea1c3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:17:21.597Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"9:## Quick start (a complete game)\n40:## Look target (read this before drawing anything)\n53:## Coordinates: what x, y, z mean in each view\n69:## Rules\n78:## Common mistakes (check these first)\n86:## Game\n102:## Scenes (title, play, game over)\n113:## Motion and timing: tweens, scripts, paths, weather\n129:## Standard features (every game has them: don't build your own)\n136:## Input: `game.input`\n146:## Drawing: `r` in `draw(r)`\n155:## Pixels, sprites, text, UI\n164:## Sound: `game.audio` (chip synth, no files, starts after the first key press)\n170:## Levels\n182:## Movement and physics\n200:## Characters\n216:## Effects and lighting\n222:## Genre playbook (NES, SNES, Genesis, N64, PS1)\n262:## More: animation and examples outside this card\n286:## Before you hand the game back\nAPI.md:94:- Methods: `follow(obj, { z: 16, lead: 20 })` (camera tracks it automatically), `focus(x, y, z)` (or aim it yourself every update), `setView(id)`, `nextView()`, `freeze(s)` (hit-stop: `update` waits; `game.hitstop` is the time left), `shake(n)`, `after(s, fn)`, `every(s, fn)` (timers in game time, return `{ cancel() }`), `mouseGround()`, `go(scene, data)`, `enableGPU({ map })`.\nAPI.md:234:| Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet, Devil's Crush) | a steep table view of its own (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1)`) | `E.Physics`: chains for the walls, `flipper`, `bumper`, `slingshot`, `kicker`, a ramp on a layer of its own, the ball a `bullet`; `input.zones` flip on a phone; `E.Arcade` for the score and table. Breakout and Asteroids with real collisions are its recipes | PINBALL |\nAPI.md:235:| Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth) | `side` at a whole scale (`new E.View(id, label, 0, 0, 1, 1)`) | `E.Terrain` (`carve` the blasts, `walk` the soldiers, `ray` the shots), grenades as `E.Physics` bodies on `land.collider()`, `E.Turns`; a drag aims (`steer = 'drag'`, `drag()`, `stickOn`); a CPU tries its shots in simulation | ARTILLERY |\nAPI-INDEX.md:221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\nAPI-INDEX.md:223:- `new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale = 1, zBoost = 1) → view`: new E.View(id, label, yaw, pitch, scale, zBoost): an orthographic camera (degrees; scale = screen pixels per world unit; zBoost stretches heights)\nAPI-INDEX.md:497:- `game.setView(v)`: switch the view: an id from E.VIEWS ('iso', 'side', ...) or a View; keeps zoom and turn\n166:- Custom: `sfx({ wave: 'square' | 'pulse' | 'pulse12' | 'triangle' | 'saw' | 'sine' | 'noise', freq: 440 or 'A4', to: 880, dur: .2, vol: .3, arp: [0, 4, 7], step: .05, vib: [8, .03] })`, or `audio.define('zap', voice)`.\n167:- Music: `music('title' | 'adventure' | 'dungeon' | 'boss' | 'victory')` (built in; any other name warns and plays nothing), or your own `{ bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [{ wave: 'square', vol: .15, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 . . . | ...' }, { wave: 'triangle', notes: '...' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s . h .' }] }`. Tokens: a note (`C4`, `F#3`, `Bb2`), `-` holds, `.` rests, `|` is ignored; drums `k s h o c t`. `music(null)` stops. `mute()`, `setVolume(0..1)` (or set `audio.musicVolume`, `sfxVolume`, then `audio.applyVolume()`), `duck(on)` (quieter music under your own pause or map screen).","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HRe5yrkDv6bT1k9xy6KvNe","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
