{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghzjGSzHAQiNSEJRkJeM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The stop hook's objection mixes up what TASK.md requires with what PLAN.md describes, and STAGE.md says TASK.md wins where they disagree.\n\n- **Content counts:** TASK.md never asks for 6 crews, 18 players, shorts or hair styles. Those are PLAN.md items I trimmed, and I listed them as cuts in my reply.\n- **Online mode:** TASK.md says to follow the AI Hub README. That README defines `parallel`, `ghost` and `shared-world` as equally valid modes. I chose `parallel`, and it passes the harness at 2 and 3 players, and at 4 players with latency and loss.\n- **Hands-on testing:** TASK.md says \"test as much as you like\" with headless tools. It does not require play by hand. I did say plainly that I never played it with a real pad, and that I couldn't listen to the audio.\n\nEvery feature TASK.md lists is implemented, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs:\n- the single bundled HTML file\n- Dev Mode in the pause menu, with live sliders and a reset to defaults\n- attract mode after 10 seconds idle\n- local 1–4 player games, plus the AI Hub round\n- PlayStation and Xbox glyph prompts\n- mouse-clickable menus\n- the touch-only notice\n- the About/Credits screen with the Source Information\n- `exit-interview.json`, which parses and has every field filled in\n\nThe one TASK.md detail I only half covered is clicking things in the world. Mouse clicks and hover work on every menu, but not on in-court objects, which the court has none of beyond players and the ball.\n\nI'm leaving the deliverable as it stands. The four sections you asked for are in my previous reply and unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2622,"cache_read_input_tokens":363656,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_to