{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghzmkGNB9KuZCpqNYgYR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The mouse hover is in, and the tests still pass. The bundled HTML was rebuilt as part of the test run.\n\n- **What's new:** In a match, moving the mouse over any player on the court shows a card with their name, player number if human, and four ratings. Left click already shoots, right click passes, and every menu responds to hover and click.\n- **How I checked it:** All 73 scripted checks pass and a browser load shows no console errors. I did not take a screenshot of the card itself, so its look and placement are untested.\n- **What's still open:** The plan's extra content stays cut, namely the 6th crew, the extra players, shorts and hair styles, and the shared-world online mode. TASK.md doesn't require any of that, and the AI Hub round runs in parallel mode. That is a gap against the plan, not against TASK.md, and I'm not going to claim the plan was met in full.\n- **What's unchanged:** `exit-interview.json` still parses and answers every field. The Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections in my earlier reply still stand."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1590,"cache_read_input_tokens":367384,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1590},"output_tokens":357,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"213edd46-9651-46f8-a282-da1d89430eab","uuid":"3fc02391-105c-4649-86bb-9fb7a0058358","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:51:18.184Z","request_id":"req_011CghzmjsoeAGbYPL1xz5WK"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The final reply the condition requires is not in the last message. The last assistant message contains no Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback or Prompt Feedback sections; it only says the earlier sections 'still stand'. The earlier reply that held them is outside the most recent turn, and the condition asks for the final reply to contain them. Also, the transcript states the plan was not fully met ('a gap against the plan'), and the stop hook has repeatedly flagged feature completeness, so 'every feature in TASK.md is implemented' is not clearly evidenced. The bundled HTML and exit-interview.json exist, and exit-interview.json was reported to parse with all fields filled."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"213edd46-9651-46f8-a282-da1d89430eab","uuid":"c7cf4604-6df7-4a74-bec8-de53587ff7b1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:51:20.663Z","isSynthetic":true}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghznBsVVK2niRRVRXDLK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The bundled single file is `Basketblam-Basketball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-061612.html` in the work folder, with `exit-interview.json` beside it, and it parses with every field filled in. 73 scripted checks pass, the browser run shows no console errors, and the AI Hub harness passes. I never played it by hand, so how the controls feel on a real pad is unchecked, and I couldn't listen to the audio.\n\nEvery feature TASK.md lists is implemented, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. The things I cut are from PLAN.md only, not TASK.md: a 6th crew and the extra players (10 players across 5 crews), the plan's shorts and hair styles, and shared-world netcode. TASK.md says to follow the AI Hub README, which allows `parallel` mode, so the online round is parallel.\n\nThe mouse works on every menu by hover and click. In a match, left click shoots and right click passes. Hovering a player on the court shows a name and ratings card; I did not screenshot that card, so its placement is untested.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:16:12\n- **Source:** Basketball (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort), built as a trimmed vertical slice\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports, 2-on-2 basketball with a four-stop story tour. Side-on broadcast camera (orthographic, pitch 30°), plus a High camera option.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified copy), AI Hub Session Client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio. Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native HD pixel style, with shaded rigs, painted court floors, tiered stands with a crowd, comic banners, and a palette and backdrop per court.\n- **Animation:** The engine's Humanoid rig system, with a pose layer for shots, dunks, swipes, shoves and spins.\n- **Audio:** All in code. Chip songs, Web Audio effects, a crowd bed, and Animalese-style gibberish voices. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode (\"BLAM SHOWDOWN\"). Everyone plays the same seeded game against a CPU crew, and the biggest point lead tops the scoreboard.\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted play-throughs (`node tests/run.mjs`, 73 checks), CPU-vs-CPU balance runs, Playwright screenshots and browser checks, the AI Hub harness. No subagents.\n- **Research:** Read the engine handoff docs, the sports kit and the AI Hub protocol. Nothing else.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 10. The steal and shove facing test was inverted, the attract mode was wired to the wrong scene, and touch-only detection never fired. Progress storage doesn't persist headless, the camera showed past the map edge, and several font glyphs rendered as \"?\". A particles call used the wrong argument order, the camp panel covered the court, the announcer box overlapped the dev panel, and the overtime test turned out flaky.\n- **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 3: steals never worked, attract mode never started, and the touch-only notice never showed. The last two are required features.\n- **Most helpful test:** The full CPU-vs-CPU game and the whole four-stop tour driven only by input taps and scene changes. They exercised every system at once, and the AI Hub harness run in the browser confirmed the online round.\n- **Least helpful test:** The static content-count checks and the determinism check. Both passed from the start and never caught anything.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The Humanoid rigs with poses, moves and live portraits. TileMap `floorTex` for painting a whole court in code. Headless `game.advance` for exact testing. The free Dialog and pause/settings screens.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Yes, several times.\n  - I guessed `particles.ring` takes `(x, y, z, …)`, but it takes `(x, y, r0, r1, color, dur, z)`.\n  - `input.lastDevice` starts as keyboard, so touch-only needs its own detection.\n  - The bitmap font has no em dash, check mark or left arrow.\n  - `E.store` doesn't persist headless.\n  - A custom `E.View` must be added to `E.VIEWS` before a Game's `views` list can name it.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** The whole basketball simulation (ball, rim and backboard physics, shot timing, dunks and alley-oops, steals, shoves, blocks), the CPU brains, and the controller-first UI.\n- **Hardest part:** Depth ordering of the hoop, net, ball and players in a low side view with `r.queue`, and keeping the camera, zoom and map edge in agreement.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** Two small changes, each marked BASKETBLAM. `Dialog.voice` may be a function so a synthesized voice speaks as lines type. `audio.sfxBus` and `audio.musicBus` are public getters so the voice and crowd follow the volume settings.\n- **One thing I'd change:** A device-seen API that starts empty, so touch-only detection and prompts don't need custom listeners.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Clear, checkable requirements, and a plan with concrete numbers that settled most design questions.\n- **Confusing:** How much of the plan is expected at medium effort. It describes far more than one session can build, and it carries file names for another model and timestamp.\n- **Hardest thing:** Choosing what to cut from a very large plan while still delivering every task feature with no stubs, and judging audio with no way to listen.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark the must-haves versus nice-to-haves, say which hub mode is acceptable, and give a content budget for the effort level."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":738,"cache_read_input_tokens":368974,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":738},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"213edd46-9651-46f8-a282-da1d89430eab","uuid":"e04dc526-4fff-4180-9847-576701adf1d4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:51:32.096Z","request_id":"req_011CghznBTgbYtvGYNbz7wEK"}
