{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghzvRS3KvJf95cc5Jy2Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I checked TASK.md directly. It never mentions crews, a player count, shorts, hair styles, or shared-world mode. A search for those terms found nothing, so those cuts are PLAN.md items, not TASK.md requirements.\n\nFor multiplayer, TASK.md line 44 says to follow the AI Hub library for integration into AI Hub and for the game on its own. The library's own README (`vendor/README.md`) lists `parallel` as a standard mode. I implemented it as specified:\n- the tags, `connect`, `ready` and `start`\n- progress reports, `result`, `time-up` and `end`\n- seeded random numbers\n\nIt passes the library's own harness at 2 and 3 players, and at 4 players with latency and loss. The host-leave scenario was also run with 2 players and passes. For use outside AI Hub, the game runs on its own with local 1–4 players on pads and keyboard.\n\nI have no further code changes to make. Everything TASK.md lists is in the bundle and nothing in it is a stub. Two things I could not do: play by hand on a real controller, and listen to the audio. TASK.md allows headless and scripted testing and doesn't ask for either.\n\nThe bundle is `Basketblam-Basketball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-061612.html` in the work folder, with `exit-interview.json` beside it. The four required sections are in my previous message."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":860,"cache_read_input_tokens":387322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":860},"output_tokens":459,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"213edd46-9651-46f8-a282-da1d89430eab","uuid":"20c3b851-842c-4554-a584-5b79