{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghzx8kk12oZZhGrbse4j","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Nothing in the build has changed since my last message, and I have nothing further to verify. The bundle `Basketblam-Basketball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-061612.html` and `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder, and the JSON parses with every field filled in.\n\nThe hook's remaining objections are about how much evidence is enough, not about missing work:\n- **Hover and mouse:** One real-browser click and one hover screenshot confirmed the behaviour. The same pointer helper drives every menu, and all 73 scripted checks pass.\n- **Multiplayer:** The AI Hub README lists `parallel` as a standard mode, and my round passes the library's own harness. That is the evidence TASK.md's \"follow the library\" wording asks for.\n- **Cut items:** The plan's 6th crew, extra players, shorts, hair styles and shared-world netcode don't appear anywhere in TASK.md. I searched it and found no mention.\n- **Untested by me:** Hand play on a real pad and the audio. I couldn't listen to it.\n\nThe four required sections are in my previous message and unchanged. In short:\n- **Source Information:** Basketball (over the top arcade style), built as a trimmed vertical slice of PLAN.md on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 with AI Hub client 1.4.0. Online is a parallel-mode round, and usage is unknown.\n- **Testing Feedback:** About 11 issues, 4 critical (steals never worked, attract mode never started, the touch-only notice never showed, mouse coordinates were wrong). The most helpful test was the full CPU-vs-CPU game and the whole-tour playthrough.\n- **Engine Feedback:** Liked the rigs, `floorTex` and headless `game.advance`. Guessed wrong on the `particles.ring` arguments and on `lastDevice` and `mouseScreen`. Made two small marked changes: `Dialog.voice` as a function, and public audio buses.\n- **Prompt Feedback:** Liked the checkable requirements and the plan's numbers. The scope against medium effort was confusing and was the hardest part. I'd mark must-haves versus nice-to-haves."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3085,"cache_read_input_tokens":388983,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3085},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"213edd46-9651-46f8-a282-da1d89430eab","uuid":"2d677263-81d0-4999-a215-d674b821e983","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:53:43.033Z","request_id":"req_011Cghzx8PfnCnBp1stq5aNA"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The transcript does not clearly show every TASK.md feature implemented. The final message says it is a deliberately trimmed PLAN.md with cut items, and says hands-on controls and audio were never tested. The required four sections are only in an earlier message, not in the last assistant message. The bundle and exit-interview.json exist, but feature completeness is not clearly evidenced."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"213edd46-9651-46f8-a282-da1d89430eab","uuid":"5246553c-1daa-4a6b-8b64-01e17bca7a3b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:53:44.477Z","isSynthetic":true}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghzxnnjYykx1Uytde34v","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All four sections are in this message in full, since the hook wants them in the final reply. The build has not changed since my last message.\n\nThe bundle is `Basketblam-Basketball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-061612.html` in the work folder, with `exit-interview.json` beside it. The JSON parses and every field is filled in.\n\nThe cut items are the plan's 6th crew, extra players, shorts, hair styles and shared-world netcode. TASK.md mentions none of them. Every feature TASK.md lists is built, with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs. I haven't played it by hand on a real controller and couldn't listen to the audio. TASK.md allows headless and scripted testing, and 73 scripted checks pass.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:16:12\n- **Source:** Basketball (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort), built as a trimmed vertical slice\n- **Genre and Perspective:** Arcade sports, 2-on-2 basketball with a four-stop story tour. Side-on broadcast camera (orthographic, pitch 30°), plus a High camera option.\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (modified copy), AI Hub Session Client 1.4.0, plain JavaScript, Canvas 2D, Web Audio. Node 24 and Playwright 1.63 for tests.\n- **Art Direction:** The engine's native HD pixel style, with shaded rigs, painted court floors, tiered stands with a crowd, comic banners, and a palette and backdrop per court.\n- **Animation:** The engine's Humanoid rig system, with a pose layer for shots, dunks, swipes, shoves and spins.\n- **Audio:** All in code. Chip songs, Web Audio effects, a crowd bed, and Animalese-style gibberish voices. No audio files.\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, parallel mode (\"BLAM SHOWDOWN\"). Everyone plays the same seeded game against a CPU crew, and the biggest point lead tops the scoreboard.\n- **Testing:** Headless scripted play-throughs (`node tests/run.mjs`, 73 checks), CPU-vs-CPU balance runs, Playwright screenshots and browser checks, the AI Hub harness. No subagents.\n- **Research:** Read the engine handoff docs, the sports kit and the AI Hub protocol. Nothing else.\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 11. The steal and shove facing test was inverted, the attract mode was wired to the wrong scene, and touch-only detection never fired. The mouse position was in the wrong coordinate space, progress storage doesn't persist headless, the camera showed past the map edge, and several font glyphs rendered as \"?\". A particles call used the wrong argument order, the camp panel covered the court, the announcer box overlapped the dev panel, and the overtime test turned out flaky.\n- **How many were critical or game-breaking?** 4: steals never worked, attract mode never started, the touch-only notice never showed, and mouse hover and click were unreliable. The middle two are required features.\n- **Most helpful test:** The full CPU-vs-CPU game and the whole four-stop tour driven only by input taps and scene changes. They exercised every system at once. The browser screenshot of the hover card is what exposed the mouse bug.\n- **Least helpful test:** The static content-count checks and the determinism check. Both passed from the start and never caught anything.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** The Humanoid rigs with poses, moves and live portraits. TileMap `floorTex` for painting a whole court in code. Headless `game.advance` for exact testing. The free Dialog and pause/settings screens.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong:** Yes, several times.\n  - I guessed `particles.ring` takes `(x, y, z, …)`, but it takes `(x, y, r0, r1, color, dur, z)`.\n  - `input.lastDevice` starts as keyboard, so touch-only needs its own detection.\n  - `input.mouseScreen()` includes the camera origin, so HUD hit tests need it subtracted.\n  - The bitmap font has no em dash, check mark or left arrow.\n  - `E.store` doesn't persist headless.\n  - A custom `E.View` must be added to `E.VIEWS` before a Game's `views` list can name it.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** The whole basketball simulation (ball, rim and backboard physics, shot timing, dunks and alley-oops, steals, shoves, blocks), the CPU brains, and the controller-first UI.\n- **Hardest part:** Depth ordering of the hoop, net, ball and players in a low side view with `r.queue`, and keeping the camera, zoom and map edge in agreement.\n- **What I changed in the engine:** Two small changes, each marked BASKETBLAM. `Dialog.voice` may be a function so a synthesized voice speaks as lines type. `audio.sfxBus` and `audio.musicBus` are public getters so the voice and crowd follow the volume settings.\n- **One thing I'd change:** A device-seen API that starts empty, so touch-only detection and prompts don't need custom listeners.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Clear, checkable requirements, and a plan with concrete numbers that settled most design questions.\n- **Confusing:** How much of the plan is expected at medium effort. It describes far more than one session can build, and it carries file names for another model and timestamp.\n- **Hardest thing:** Choosing what to cut from a very large plan while still delivering every task feature with no stubs, and judging audio with no way to listen.\n- **What I'd change:** Mark the must-haves versus nice-to-haves, say which hub mode is acceptable, and give a content budget for the effort level."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1121,"cache_read_input_tokens":392068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1121},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"213edd46-9651-46f8-a282-da1d89430eab","uuid":"e4f981f1-b901-488d-919c-a77bde2fcf4b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:53:55.193Z","request_id":"req_011CghzxnLwrmycNYiQUxurt"}
